ution for it  happening I it just softened her all the  more number nine mance rayder this is a  case where this is a guy who we've heard  so much about but seen so little of he's  well cast and thankfully they cast guy  who's got a certain amount of screen  presence and a certain amount of Menace  and he helps sell it as best as it can  be sold but it's just we spent so much  time hearing about him before we  saw him and then when we saw him and  then he vanished for so long and again  we keep hearing about him but everybody  talking about how dangerous or how  influential and somebody is as opposed  to actually showing us that that's a  problem and it just makes the character  not stick and not have the resonance  that he probably should have I mean he  should feel like a threat he should feel  like a pretty big problem honestly he  feels more like an annoyance that I wish  the show would just kind of wrap up and  deal with already so we can get on to  different stuff  number eight Daario naharis now this is  really a criticism of the recast Daario  naharis the original guy that they had  when he showed up in season 3 I actually  really liked cuz he was a little bit odd  it kind of in the same way that the  faceless assassin was on and that he  couldn't quite pin him down you're like  I think this is kind of your deal but I  was intrigued by him the recast version  of Dyer and the horrors I'm not  intrigued by I feel like I can read him  like a book and he's just been played  very much straight that he is enamored  with Daenerys when it the stuff was  going on in season 3 he was saying that  and you got that aspect it felt like  there was something else that I couldn't  quite pin down and I liked that and that  that now feels gone with the new guy and  I'm just gonna put that down to the  performance I just think that the guy  that they got to replace the original  actor just isn't bringing as many layers  to the character he's playing it  straight and played stra